 comparison for this caption; no absence proof from failed search."}, "evidence_origin": [{"origin": "new_comparison", "ref": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/kingsday_xml_104682.json", "claims_resolved": ["Caption-to-object and page association from packet; caption-specific visual observation using view_image", "Document combines limited vertical advection correction and implicit pressure difference. The active one-layer predictor calls advW after explicit pressure; corrector solves dp and updates pressure/velocities. Term coefficient, pressure normalization and reported time labels were not shown identical; no full mapping claimed."], "gaps_left": ["Document combines limited vertical advection correction and implicit pressure difference. The active one-layer predictor calls advW after explicit pressure; corrector solves dp and updates pressure/velocities. Term coefficient, pressure normalization and reported time labels were not shown identical; no full mapping claimed."]}], "document_differences": [], "symbols": [{"symbol": "W̄", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 104051}, "definition_quote": "The pressures are defined on the cell faces and therefore do not have to be interpolated. Furthermore, we can exactly set the dynamic pressure at the free surface  to zero. The vertical velocities are defined on the cell faces and therefore the depth averaged velocity  needs to be expressed in terms of the bottom and surface velocities. Using a simple central approximation gives", "meaning": "depth averaged vertical velocity; capital bare W is not explicitly defined here"}, {"symbol": "ΔW̄", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document", "context_basis": {"meaning": "face slope-limited W̄ increments by analogy with B.61", "reference": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 104738}, "quote": "Where  and  are obtained using relations similar to . Note that similar to  and again the kinematic boundary conditions is substituted for .", "limit": "This reference does not print a complete explicit definition."}, "context_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 104738}, "definition_search": {"document": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "scope": "all paragraph w:t including symbol/output tables, coordinate definitions and the opened local equations/inline formulas", "result": "No explicit occurrence-appropriate definition of this exact printed symbol located; context/source meanings and spelling variants are separated."}}, {"symbol": "H", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 100959}, "definition_quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "meaning": "water depth"}, {"symbol": "q^x", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 101135}, "definition_quote": "With ^x q^*_{i+1/2,j}=H^n_{i+1/2,j}U^{n+1/2}_{i+1/2,j}", "meaning": "x depth-integrated discharge defined by H U"}, {"symbol": "q^y", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 101135}, "definition_quote": "^y q^*_{i,j+1/2}=H^n_{i,j+1/2}V^{n+1/2}_{i,j+1/2}", "meaning": "y depth-integrated discharge defined by H V"}, {"symbol": "Δp", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 102443}, "definition_quote": "p^{n+1½}_{i,j}=p^{n+1/2}_{i,j}+Δp^{n+1½}_{i,j}", "meaning": "pressure increment in the explicit pressure decomposition (B.55); normalization not supplied by this definition", "context_basis": {"method": "opened render image", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/kingsday/page-141.png", "sha256": "91548b300fd626cef484ce1cfb809b78cb56371c3b44830981f2a2fe73377437", "paragraph": 102443}}, {"symbol": "Δt", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 95916}, "definition_quote": "In  the pressure term plpf  is the surface water pressure at the bed, which in the case of non-hydrostatic surface water flow is high-pass filtered at 4/Trep, the superscript n corresponds to the time step number and Δt is the size of the time step. The infiltration rate in the coupled relationship can be solved through substitution:", "meaning": "size of time step"}, {"symbol": "Δx", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document", "context_basis": {"meaning": "x grid spacing in the printed finite differences", "limit": "Standard/source-supported role, not a located explicit definition for this exact printed symbol."}, "definition_search": {"document": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "scope": "all paragraph w:t including symbol/output tables, coordinate definitions and the opened local equations/inline formulas", "result": "No explicit occurrence-appropriate definition of this exact printed symbol located; context/source meanings and spelling variants are separated."}}, {"symbol": "Δy", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document", "context_basis": {"meaning": "y grid spacing in the printed finite differences", "limit": "Standard/source-supported role, not a located explicit definition for this exact printed symbol."}, "definition_search": {"document": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "scope": "all paragraph w:t including symbol/output tables, coordinate definitions and the opened local equations/inline formulas", "result": "No explicit occurrence-appropriate definition of this exact printed symbol located; context/source meanings and spelling variants are separated."}}, {"symbol": "n", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 94025}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "time step index in discretized equations; not the group velocity ratio output variable"}, {"symbol": "i,j", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 94025}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "grid number in u and v directions; (B.43) uses bed-layer/sediment-class indices instead"}, {"symbol": "*", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document", "context_basis": {"meaning": "predicted/intermediate-state label in this local scheme", "limit": "Standard/source-supported role, not a located explicit definition for this exact printed symbol."}, "definition_search": {"document": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "scope": "all paragraph w:t including symbol/output tables, coordinate definitions and the opened local equations/inline formulas", "result": "No explicit occurrence-appropriate definition of this exact printed symbol located; context/source meanings and spelling variants are separated."}}], "evidence": [{"role": "receipt", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/kingsday_xml_104682.json", "line_start": 26, "line_end": 26, "quote": "      \"text\": \"(B.67)\"", "sha256": "18871336e351bfed046daf9603a1c27fc997292e3d058292bd8eba201d285955"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 1234, "line_end": 1261, "quote": "      !Include explicit approximation for pressure in s%uu and s%vv   and Wm\n      if (par%secorder == 1) then\n         do j=jmin,jmax\n            do i=imin_uu,imax_uu\n               s%uu(i,j) = s%uu(i,j) + au(1,i,j) * s%pres(i+1,j) + au(0,i,j) * s%pres(i  ,j)\n            enddo\n         enddo\n\n         if (s%ny>0) then\n            do j=jmin_vv,jmax_vv\n               do i=imin_vv,imax_vv\n                  s%vv(i,j) = s%vv(i,j) + av(1,i,j) * s%pres(i,j+1) + av(0,i,j) * s%pres(i,j  )\n               enddo\n            enddo\n         else\n            do i=imin_vv,imax_vv\n               s%vv(i,1) = s%vv(i,1) + av(1,i,1) * s%pres(i,1) + av(0,i,1) * s%pres(i,1  )\n            enddo\n         endif\n\n         do j=jmin_zs,jmax_zs\n            do i=imin_zs,imax_zs\n               if (nonhZ(i,j) == 1) then\n                  Wm(i,j) = Wm(i,j)   + Wcoef(i,j)*par%dt * s%pres(i,j)/s%hh(i,j)\n               endif\n            enddo\n         enddo\n         call flow_secondorder_advW(s,par,Wm,Wm_old, nonhZ)", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 683, "line_end": 690, "quote": "      !Solve matrix\n      !call timer_start(timer_flow_nonh_solv)\n      dp = 0.0_rKind\n      call solver_solvemat( mat  , rhs   , dp , s%nx, s%ny,par)\n      !call timer_stop(timer_flow_nonh_solv)\n\n\n      s%pres = s%pres + dp", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_secondorder.F90", "line_start": 518, "line_end": 526, "quote": "                     delta1    = (w(ie,j ) - w_old(i  ,j )) / s%dsu(i,j)\n                     delta2    = (w(i,j )  - w_old(iw ,j )) / s%dsu(iw,j)\n                     wrk1(i,j)   = 0.5d0*s%dsu(i,j)*minmod(delta1,delta2) * qx\n                     !\n                  elseif (qx < 0.0_rKind .and. i<imax) then\n                     !\n                     delta1    = (w_old(ie ,j)  - w(i ,j )) / s%dsu(i,j)\n                     delta2    = (w_old(iee,j ) - w(ie,j )) / s%dsu(ie,j)\n                     wrk1(i,j) = -0.5d0*s%dsu(i,j)*minmod(delta1,delta2)*qx", "sha256": "33d588f751f2faffb02b0c97854a0a975f67ab7851492d7927c8ff68d545b3de"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "The pressures are defined on the cell faces and therefore do not have to be interpolated. Furthermore, we can exactly set the dynamic pressure at the free surface  to zero. The vertical velocities are defined on the cell faces and therefore the depth averaged velocity  needs to be expressed in terms of the bottom and surface velocities. Using a simple central approximation gives", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 104051}, "quote_method": "Source DOCX defining paragraph w:t; inline q definitions separately transcribed from an opened image."}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 100959}, "quote_method": "Source DOCX defining paragraph w:t; inline q definitions separately transcribed from an opened image."}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "With ^x q^*_{i+1/2,j}=H^n_{i+1/2,j}U^{n+1/2}_{i+1/2,j}", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 101135}, "quote_method": "Source DOCX defining paragraph w:t; inline q definitions separately transcribed from an opened image."}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "^y q^*_{i,j+1/2}=H^n_{i,j+1/2}V^{n+1/2}_{i,j+1/2}", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 101135}, "quote_method": "Source DOCX defining paragraph w:t; inline q definitions separately transcribed from an opened image."}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "In  the pressure term plpf  is the surface water pressure at the bed, which in the case of non-hydrostatic surface water flow is high-pass filtered at 4/Trep, the superscript n corresponds to the time step number and Δt is the size of the time step. The infiltration rate in the coupled relationship can be solved through substitution:", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 95916}, "quote_method": "Source DOCX defining paragraph w:t; inline q definitions separately transcribed from an opened image."}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 94025}, "quote_method": "Source DOCX defining paragraph w:t; inline q definitions separately transcribed from an opened image."}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 94025}, "quote_method": "Source DOCX defining paragraph w:t; inline q definitions separately transcribed from an opened image."}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "Where  and  are obtained using relations similar to . Note that similar to  and again the kinematic boundary conditions is substituted for .", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 104738}, "quote_method": "Verbatim w:t in the defining DOCX paragraph"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "p^{n+1½}_{i,j}=p^{n+1/2}_{i,j}+Δp^{n+1½}_{i,j}", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 102443}, "quote_method": "Visual transcription of defining formula on opened render image; inline OLE is absent from w:t", "visual_image": {"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/kingsday/page-141.png", "sha256": "91548b300fd626cef484ce1cfb809b78cb56371c3b44830981f2a2fe73377437"}}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "where the difference in pressure is generally small. In the predictor step the effect of the pressure is included explicitly using. In the corrector step the full Poisson equation is then solved for . The pressure term in the predictor step is thus given as:", "sha256": "c78396a23cec17b13be94ab1deef921c89b3d0c6a3d1f7d05e7d741e432c6543", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_start_xml_ordinal": 102525}, "quote_method": "Verbatim w:t in the defining DOCX paragraph"}], "differences": ["Source uses Wcoef and nonhZ masks and calls advW in nonh_1lay_pred, rather than proving the combined displayed corrector at this exact time level."], "closure_status": "unresolved", "note": "Document combines limited vertical advection correction and implicit pressure difference. The active one-layer predictor calls advW after explicit pressure; corrector solves dp and updates pressure/velocities. Term coefficient, pressure normalization and reported time labels were not shown identical; no full mapping claimed. Association adapter compatibility: packet has no top-level objects[].member, so member=null preserves that supplied value; actual ZIP member remains explicitly in ole.member and relationship.member together with original locator and SHA256. Paragraph xml:104738 defines the face-increment construction by reference to B.61, rather than supplying an independent expanded ΔW̄ formula; this link does not settle the implementation/time-level gaps. S1 delimitation of the NARROWED fix: xml:104738 is a construction reference to relations similar to B.61, not a complete definition; its link is retained as context_locator and definition_locator remains null. S1 audit: reviewed defining paragraphs/equations and searched the entire document paragraph text, including output-symbol tables; rechecked every undefined entry against local opened formulas. Introductions and analogous-construction references are context, not standalone explicit definitions. Document observation (S2): B.67 prints n+1½ on corrected W̄ and Δp; the following text gives an analogous-construction reference for face ΔW̄."}
{"id": "master:xml:96732", "association": {"status": "unique", "objects": [{"kind": "ole", "locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "xml_ordinal": 96720, "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 96704}, "relationship": {"id": "rId443", "target": "embeddings/oleObject200.bin", "type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/oleObject", "member": "word/embeddings/oleObject200.bin"}, "ole": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx!word/embeddings/oleObject200.bin", "storage": "zip-member", "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/embeddings/oleObject200.bin", "sha256": "60fecb78ce11d1e1af220d539ad119725f75c6981f87cbde1d77a93abf80742e"}, "prog_id": "Equation.DSMT4", "shape_id": "_x0000_i1224", "object_id": "_1492332817", "previews": [{"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx!word/media/image224.wmf", "storage": "zip-member", "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/media/image224.wmf", "sha256": "bebd2d9baeae2138196c36e4177d247f839dd08e2a08a486c59d6685bd806bca", "relationship": {"id": "rId442", "target": "media/image224.wmf", "type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image", "member": "word/media/image224.wmf"}, "xml_ordinal": 96719}], "preview_binding_status": "unique", "member": null}], "page": 144}, "body_status": "readable", "equation_content": {"images_used": [{"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/master/page-144.png", "region": "Equation (C.54) at its printed caption; full existing render page", "sha256": "6f4e82cee387828dda3cbe768e6a3d196caa31f5d4d442b6987a00875abc4edc"}], "transcription": "{}^{x}T_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2} = (2/Δx_{i+1/2})[ν_{i+1,j}^{n}H_{i+1,j}^{n+1}(U_{i+1½,j}^{n+1/2}−U_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2})/Δx_{i+1} − ν_{i,j}^{n}H_{i,j}^{n+1}(U_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2}−U_{i−1/2,j}^{n+1/2})/Δx_i] + (1/Δy_i)[ν̄_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{n+1/2}H̿_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{n+1/2}(U_{i+1/2,j+1}^{n+1}−U_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2})/Δy_{i+1/2} − ν̄_{i+1/2,j−1/2}^{n+1/2}H̿_{i+1/2,j−1/2}^{n+1}(U_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2}−U_{i+1/2,j−1}^{n+1/2})/Δy_{i−1/2}] + (1/Δy_i)[ν̿_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{n+1/2}H̿_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{n+1/2}(V_{i+1,j+1/2}^{n+1}−V_{i,j+1/2}^{n+1/2})/Δx_{i+1/2} − ν̿_{i+1/2,j−1/2}^{n+1/2}H̿_{i+1/2,j−1/2}^{n+1}(V_{i+1,j−1/2}^{n+1/2}−V_{i,j−1/2}^{n+1/2})/Δx_{i+1/2}]", "uncertain_symbols": [], "reviewer_note": "Reopened the listed existing page images with tools.view_image for this correction. This is a visual transcription, separate from the document-text quotes. Left superscripts are written {}^{x}, {}^{y}, {}^{w}, or {}^{u}; q is lowercase, q̄/W̄ have a single overbar and ν̿/H̿ a double overbar. Every printed time and spatial index is retained; no α/β abbreviation or normalization is used. Document observations: The first forward U and V factors in the two y brackets have n+1, while the backward factors have n+½. H double bars and different time levels n+½/n+1 are preserved. The ν overbar in the U_y bracket is single; in the V_x bracket it is double. The first U spatial subscript is printed i+1½. Δy_i and Δy_{i±½} are printed as such."}, "document_role": "model_relation", "implementation_relation": "unresolved", "evidence_origin": [{"origin": "new_comparison", "ref": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/master_xml_96732.json", "claims_resolved": ["Actual visual body at (C.54); document text quotes and defining symbol links rechecked", "Bounded source comparison with the term/stage/sign limits stated in note"], "gaps_left": ["T/H maps to viscu: x normal strain, y U gradient and y divergence of V_x. Differences: source multiplies the initial normal component by 2 only for smag==1 and includes V_x cross term only for smag==1; uses metric spacings, wet masks and four-point ν averaging. ν is supplied by viscosity-off=0, Smagorinsky or par%nuh with nhbreaker-dependent increments, and subsequently scaled by nuhv before the vertical nonh predictor. Printed mixed-stage/time details are recorded as document observations; no exact stencil equality claimed. Source evidence locators: models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:365-404; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:411-464; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:496-496. No silent ν=ν_h, W=wind-speed W, or d=−zb document-definition substitution is made; source/context meaning is distinguished from missing document definition. Association unchanged. Packet objects have no top-level member field; member=null preserves that shape, while actual ZIP member, relationship, locator and hashes are retained in relationship/ole/previews. Independent correction: NARROWED confirmed against the opened equation page and source/context; 인용문을 재추출한다. 명시된 전사 불확실성과 구현 조건은 유지한다. S1 full-document text search plus visible nomenclature/defining-equation review: remaining undefined_in_document symbols are ν, Δx, Δy. Their standard meanings or supplied source context alone are documentation limits; substantive pressure, boundary, placement or implementation gaps remain unresolved where stated. Bare ν in the turbulent-stress equation is not silently identified with ν_h at @20451 or the water kinematic viscosity ν at @25292; those define different notation/context. The additional confirmed n+1/n+½ asymmetry in the transverse U and V factors is not explained by the source, which uses the supplied s%uu/s%vv fields at a single assembled stage (flow_timestep.F90:445-462). Thus exact literal mixed-stage stencil meaning remains unresolved even though central viscous terms have source counterparts."]}, {"origin": "existing_contract", "ref": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/build-mode-20260912/contracts.json#/modes/3", "claims_resolved": ["WAVEMODEL_NONH/nonhq3d!=1 dispatches old one-layer predictor then UV advection correction then pressure corrector"], "gaps_left": ["This dispatch contract does not adjudicate individual equation terms, indices, signs or coefficients"]}], "document_differences": [], "symbols": [{"symbol": "T", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 96639, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here Pr represents a discretization of the dynamic pressure; T the effect of (turbulent) viscosity and S includes all other source terms. The discretization of the (turbulent) viscous terms is given by central differences:", "meaning": "turbulent/viscous contribution"}, {"symbol": "ν", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "H", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 95357, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "meaning": "water depth"}, {"symbol": "U", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 95357, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "meaning": "depth-averaged x velocity"}, {"symbol": "V", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 95357, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "meaning": "depth-averaged y velocity"}, {"symbol": "Δx", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "Δy", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "i", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "grid number in u direction"}, {"symbol": "j", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "grid number in v direction"}, {"symbol": "n", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "time-step index"}], "evidence": [{"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/master/display-recovered/render.txt", "line_start": 7504, "line_end": 7514, "quote": "      transitions between the boundary condition files may affect the model results.\n      Every time the XBeach wave boundary condition module is run, it outputs data to the local\n      directory. Metadata about the wave boundary conditions are stored in list files: ebcflist.bcf and\n      qbcflist.bcf. The main XBeach program uses the list files to know how and when to read and\n      generate boundary condition files. The actual incoming short-wave energy and long-wave\n      mass flux data is stored in other files. These files have E_ and q_ prefixes. The main XBeach\n      program uses these files for the actual forcing along the offshore edge.\n\n\n\n", "sha256": "3a455dff9ca9050757471e774527dd569733659c89b8a5961c3b25e0c195092d"}, {"role": "receipt", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/master_xml_96732.json", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 12, "quote": "{\n  \"schema\": \"xbeach-r2-evidence-packet/v1\",\n  \"caption\": {\n    \"id\": \"master:xml:96732\",\n    \"document\": \"master\",\n    \"label\": \"(C.54)\",\n    \"locator_kind\": \"start_xml_ordinal\",\n    \"locator\": 96732,\n    \"source\": {\n      \"path\": \"models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx\",\n      \"sha256\": \"9f142b89e0659e71066054c3d61b4d6f29ba3c10c5984e26e9a2d37d2fae3236\"\n    },", "sha256": "5bd64e03e928694f5217e0d1b71a8c1aeca68eee9a0fc125053e6060cb1094db"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90", "line_start": 365, "line_end": 404, "quote": "      ! There is a possibility to turn viscosity off\n      if (par%viscosity==0) then ! Dano: put it here so it actualy saves a lot of computation time\n         s%nuh = 0.d0\n         s%viscu = 0.d0\n      else\n\n         ! Jaap: Slightly changes approach; 1) background viscosity is user defined or obtained from Smagorinsky, 2) nuh = max(nuh,roller induced viscosity)\n         if (par%smag == 1) then\n            !Use smagorinsky subgrid model\n            call visc_smagorinsky(s,par)\n         else\n            s%nuh = par%nuh\n         endif\n         !\n         ! Add viscosity for wave breaking effects\n         if (par%swave == 1) then\n            if (par%smag==0) then ! approach of Reniers seems inconsistent with Smagorinski\n               do j=j1,max(s%ny,1)\n                  do i=2,s%nx\n                     s%nuh(i,j) = max(s%nuh(i,j),par%nuhfac*s%hh(i,j)*(s%DR(i,j)/par%rho)**(1.0d0/3.0d0)) ! Ad: change to max\n                  end do\n               end do\n            endif\n         elseif (par%swave==0 .and. par%wavemodel==WAVEMODEL_NONH) then\n            select case (par%nhbreaker)\n             case (1)\n               where (s%breaking/=0)\n                  s%nuh = par%breakviscfac*s%nuh\n               endwhere\n             case (2)\n               where (s%breaking==1)\n                  s%nuh = s%nuh + (par%nuh*par%breakvisclen*s%hh)**2*sqrt(dudx**2+dvdy**2)\n               endwhere\n             case (3)\n               ! Ad en Arnold: Battjes 1975 formulation to smoothen front of lf wave bore in the swash\n               ! compute (long) wave turbulence due to breaking\n               !nuh = max(par%nuh, par%avis*hloc*sqrt(kturb))\n             case default\n               ! do nothing to increase viscosity\n            end select", "sha256": "50742b601cc8feccd513cf742ca772b6021f1d4f5ffe074c4e8ffc90907dd2b2"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90", "line_start": 411, "line_end": 464, "quote": "               dudx1 = s%nuh(i+1,j)*s%hh(i+1,j)*(s%uu(i+1,j)-s%uu(i,j))/s%dsz(i+1,j)\n               dudx2 = s%nuh(i,j)  *s%hh(i  ,j)*(s%uu(i,j)-s%uu(i-1,j))/s%dsz(i,j)\n               s%viscu(i,j) = (1.0d0/s%hum(i,j))*( 2*(dudx1-dudx2)/(s%dsz(i,j)+s%dsz(i+1,j)) )\n            end do\n         end do\n\n         if (par%smag == 1) then\n            !\n            !   For non constant eddy viscosity the stress terms read:\n            !\n            !   d           d           d      d         d\n            !   -- [ 2* mu -- (U) ]  + --[ mu --(U) +mu --(V) ]\n            !   dx         dx          dy     dy        dx\n            !\n            !                d         d\n            !   Only when   -- [mu] = --[mu] = 0 we have (for incompressible flow)\n            !               dx        dy\n            !\n            !         2            2\n            !        d            d\n            !    mu --2 [U] + mu --2 [U]\n            !       dx           dy\n            !\n            s%viscu = 2.0d0*s%viscu\n         endif\n\n         do j=jmin_uu,jmax_uu\n            jp1=min(j+1,s%ny+1)\n            jm1=max(j-1,1)\n            do i=imin_uu,imax_uu\n               !Nuh is defined at eta points, interpolate from four surrounding points\n               nuh1  = .25d0*(s%nuh(i,j)+s%nuh(i+1,j)+s%nuh(i+1,jp1)+s%nuh(i,jp1))\n               nuh2  = .25d0*(s%nuh(i,j)+s%nuh(i+1,j)+s%nuh(i+1,jm1)+s%nuh(i,jm1))\n\n               dudy1 = nuh1 *.5d0*(s%hvm(i,j  )+s%hvm(i+1,j  ))*(s%uu(i,jp1)-s%uu(i,j))/s%dnc(i,j)\n               dudy2 = nuh2 *.5d0*(s%hvm(i,jm1)+s%hvm(i+1,jm1))*(s%uu(i,j)-s%uu(i,jm1))/s%dnc(i,jm1)\n               s%viscu(i,j) = s%viscu(i,j) + (1.0d0/s%hum(i,j))* &\n               ( 2.0d0*(dudy1-dudy2)/(s%dnc(i,j)+s%dnc(i,jm1)) )*s%wetu(i,jp1)*s%wetu(i,jm1)\n            end do\n         end do\n\n         if (par%smag == 1) then\n            do j=jmin_uu,jmax_uu\n               jp1=min(j+1,s%ny+1)\n               jm1=max(j-1,1)\n               do i=imin_uu,imax_uu\n                  !Nuh is defined at eta points, interpolate from four surrounding points\n                  nuh1  = .25d0*(s%nuh(i,j)+s%nuh(i+1,j)+s%nuh(i+1,jp1)+s%nuh(i,jp1))\n                  nuh2  = .25d0*(s%nuh(i,j)+s%nuh(i+1,j)+s%nuh(i+1,jm1)+s%nuh(i,jm1))\n\n                  dvdx1 = nuh1*.5d0*(s%hvm(i,j  )+s%hvm(i+1,j  ))*(s%vv(i+1,j  )-s%vv(i,j  ))/s%dsc(i,j)\n                  dvdx2 = nuh2*.5d0*(s%hvm(i,jm1)+s%hvm(i+1,jm1))*(s%vv(i+1,jm1)-s%vv(i,jm1))/s%dsc(i,jm1)\n                  s%viscu(i,j) = s%viscu(i,j) + (1.d0/s%hum(i,j))*(dvdx1-dvdx2)/s%dnz(i,j)*real(s%wetv(i+1,j) &\n                  * s%wetv(i,j)*s%wetv(i+1,jm1)*s%wetv(i,jm1),8)", "sha256": "50742b601cc8feccd513cf742ca772b6021f1d4f5ffe074c4e8ffc90907dd2b2"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90", "line_start": 496, "line_end": 496, "quote": "         s%nuh = par%nuhv*s%nuh !Robert en Ap: increase s%nuh interaction in d2v/dx2", "sha256": "50742b601cc8feccd513cf742ca772b6021f1d4f5ffe074c4e8ffc90907dd2b2"}, {"role": "contract", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/build-mode-20260912/contracts.json", "line_start": 40, "line_end": 49, "quote": "      \"id\": \"nonh_one_layer\",\n      \"guard\": \"wavemodel==NONH and nonhq3d!=1\",\n      \"sequence\": [\n        \"flow\",\n        \"nonh_cor(0) -> nonh_1lay_pred\",\n        \"flow_secondorder_advUV\",\n        \"nonh_cor(1) -> nonh_1lay_cor\"\n      ],\n      \"update_guard\": \"each successful physics step; input validation turns secorder on\"\n    },", "sha256": "5cf1339c508a60d2bfaedc17f0863f16a155df70d45159f8de8dea3fd0f2a0f6"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 233, "line_end": 243, "quote": "       case default\n         !\n         ! The \"old\" code is used\n         !\n         if ( ipredcor == 0 ) then\n            ! -- Predictor\n            call nonh_1lay_pred(s,par)\n            !\n         else\n            ! -- Corrector\n            call nonh_1lay_cor(s,par)", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90", "line_start": 635, "line_end": 658, "quote": "      if (par%wavemodel==WAVEMODEL_NONH) then\n         !Do explicit predictor step with pressure\n         call nonh_cor(s,par,0,uu_old,vv_old)\n\n#ifdef USEMPI\n         call xmpi_shift_ee(s%uu)\n         call xmpi_shift_ee(s%vv)\n#endif\n      end if\n\n      if (par%secorder==1) then\n         !Call second order correction to the advection\n         call flow_secondorder_advUV(s,par,uu_old,vv_old)\n#ifdef USEMPI\n         call xmpi_shift_ee(s%uu)\n         call xmpi_shift_ee(s%vv)\n#endif\n      end if\n\n      if (par%wavemodel==WAVEMODEL_NONH) then\n         ! do non-hydrostatic pressure compensation to solve short waves\n         call nonh_cor(s,par,1,uu_old,vv_old)\n         ! note: MPI shift in subroutine nonh_cor\n      end if", "sha256": "50742b601cc8feccd513cf742ca772b6021f1d4f5ffe074c4e8ffc90907dd2b2"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "Here Pr represents a discretization of the dynamic pressure; T the effect of (turbulent) viscosity and S includes all other source terms. The discretization of the (turbulent) viscous terms is given by central differences:", "sha256": "9f142b89e0659e71066054c3d61b4d6f29ba3c10c5984e26e9a2d37d2fae3236", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 96639, "kind": "paragraph"}}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "sha256": "9f142b89e0659e71066054c3d61b4d6f29ba3c10c5984e26e9a2d37d2fae3236", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 95357, "kind": "paragraph"}}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "sha256": "9f142b89e0659e71066054c3d61b4d6f29ba3c10c5984e26e9a2d37d2fae3236", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}}], "closure_status": "unresolved", "note": "T/H maps to viscu: x normal strain, y U gradient and y divergence of V_x. Differences: source multiplies the initial normal component by 2 only for smag==1 and includes V_x cross term only for smag==1; uses metric spacings, wet masks and four-point ν averaging. ν is supplied by viscosity-off=0, Smagorinsky or par%nuh with nhbreaker-dependent increments, and subsequently scaled by nuhv before the vertical nonh predictor. Printed mixed-stage/time details are recorded as document observations; no exact stencil equality claimed. Source evidence locators: models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:365-404; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:411-464; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:496-496. No silent ν=ν_h, W=wind-speed W, or d=−zb document-definition substitution is made; source/context meaning is distinguished from missing document definition. Association unchanged. Packet objects have no top-level member field; member=null preserves that shape, while actual ZIP member, relationship, locator and hashes are retained in relationship/ole/previews. Independent correction: NARROWED confirmed against the opened equation page and source/context; 인용문을 재추출한다. 명시된 전사 불확실성과 구현 조건은 유지한다. S1 full-document text search plus visible nomenclature/defining-equation review: remaining undefined_in_document symbols are ν, Δx, Δy. Their standard meanings or supplied source context alone are documentation limits; substantive pressure, boundary, placement or implementation gaps remain unresolved where stated. Bare ν in the turbulent-stress equation is not silently identified with ν_h at @20451 or the water kinematic viscosity ν at @25292; those define different notation/context. The additional confirmed n+1/n+½ asymmetry in the transverse U and V factors is not explained by the source, which uses the supplied s%uu/s%vv fields at a single assembled stage (flow_timestep.F90:445-462). Thus exact literal mixed-stage stencil meaning remains unresolved even though central viscous terms have source counterparts.", "differences": ["source multiplies the initial normal component by 2 only for smag==1 and includes V_x cross term only for smag==1; uses metric spacings, wet masks and four-point ν averaging. ν is supplied by viscosity-off=0, Smagorinsky or par%nuh with nhbreaker-dependent increments, and subsequently scaled by nuhv before the vertical nonh predictor. Printed mixed-stage stencil observations are recorded in document_observations; their meaning remains unexplained."], "document_observations": ["The first forward U and V factors in the two y brackets have n+1, while the backward factors have n+½. H double bars and different time levels n+½/n+1 are preserved. The ν overbar in the U_y bracket is single; in the V_x bracket it is double. The first U spatial subscript is printed i+1½. Δy_i and Δy_{i±½} are printed as such."]}
{"id": "nonhydro:word:106173", "association": {"status": "unique", "objects": [{"kind": "ole", "locator": {"container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "xml_ordinal": 16322, "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 16290}, "relationship": {"id": "rId502", "target": "embeddings/oleObject237.bin", "type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/oleObject", "member": "word/embeddings/oleObject237.bin"}, "ole": {"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx!word/embeddings/oleObject237.bin", "storage": "zip-member", "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "member": "word/embeddings/oleObject237.bin", "sha256": "71a70ae0a3954d97ec20aec318eb3e6afaba3e41a7d8c22def9517e7b6b4b259"}, "prog_id": "", "shape_id": "ole_rId502", "object_id": "_976602778", "previews": [{"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx!word/media/image216.wmf", "storage": "zip-member", "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "member": "word/media/image216.wmf", "sha256": "a430e3dc12627fcf43d06f065ecad297974a6731c0c5266244311949368b1759", "relationship": {"id": "rId503", "target": "media/image216.wmf", "type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image", "member": "word/media/image216.wmf"}, "xml_ordinal": 16321}], "preview_binding_status": "unique", "original_stream_identity": {"source": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/reports/non-hydrostatic_report_draft.doc", "sha256": "07428e686eb4d2211448dcae7b7f77cdae8281affa020f68dacf42df19aa19ec"}, "native_sha256": "5433cad3e9f1adda142344d1782b3f35df17c9e8bcb1ecc9f277ffbf4ed86e0c", "candidate_stream_locators": [["ObjectPool", "_1322997946", "Equation Native"]], "method": "Opaque Equation Native byte SHA only; does not choose caption occurrence."}, "member": null}], "page": 28}, "body_status": "readable", "equation_content": {"images_used": [{"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-28.png", "region": "caption (2.30), physical render page 28", "sha256": "a78228bb228076950e8920a729909cf1ed38f0effc05990b6a0070607a0b6eeb"}, {"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-06.png", "region": "defining nomenclature/prose for symbols in this equation", "sha256": "1cd46d9a237e9ddede36b24afb8e5e7b7f706abd687d5093717879815f73950c"}, {"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-07.png", "region": "defining nomenclature/prose for symbols in this equation", "sha256": "167a275bb8b874119efc705affe340e5d8ddd72170b2732b44cd67d624942232"}], "transcription": "∂U^r/∂t - c ∂U^r/∂x = 0", "uncertain_symbols": [], "reviewer_note": "Correction pass: render page opened with tools.view_image at original resolution where needed; selected details enlarged in memory without writing an image. AI visual transcription, not mathematical verification. Left superscripts, mixed printed time labels, bars, case and grid indices are retained. Printed oddities are recorded under document_observations."}, "document_role": "definition_or_assumption", "implementation_relation": "not_applicable", "evidence_origin": [{"origin": "new_comparison", "ref": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/nonhydro_word_106173.json + opened render page 28", "claims_resolved": ["caption/object/page identity retained from packet", "individual visual reading or explicitly partial reading", "document role and symbol-definition locators checked"], "gaps_left": ["notation/document-definition or implementation differences listed in symbols and note"]}, {"origin": "new_comparison", "ref": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/nonhydro_word_106173.json; correction pass image/source review", "claims_resolved": ["individual caption image reopened", "literal transcription rechecked and printed observations separated from implementation claims"], "gaps_left": ["retained closure gaps in note and undefined symbol entries; this review does not infer missing author intent"]}], "document_differences": [], "symbols": [{"symbol": "U", "definition_locator": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.txt:144-144; List of Main symbols, italic U entry", "definition_quote": "x-component of the depth averaged velocity U", "meaning": "x component of depth-averaged velocity"}, {"symbol": "c", "definition_locator": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.txt:1100-1101; where paragraph after (2.30)", "definition_quote": "where c is the shallow water wave celerity.", "meaning": "shallow-water wave celerity"}, {"symbol": "t", "definition_locator": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.txt:139-139; List of Main symbols, t entry", "definition_quote": "Time", "meaning": "time"}, {"symbol": "x", "definition_locator": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.txt:159-159; List of Main symbols, x entry", "definition_quote": "Principle horizontal coordinate", "meaning": "primary horizontal coordinate"}, {"symbol": "r (reflected)", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}], "evidence": [{"role": "receipt", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/nonhydro_word_106173.json", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 204, "quote": "", "sha256": "d512b413f06833373db35f55bef872e932f1a762e5ffc45c4a3bc7b6e99c6b67"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-06.png", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "", "sha256": "1cd46d9a237e9ddede36b24afb8e5e7b7f706abd687d5093717879815f73950c"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-07.png", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "", "sha256": "167a275bb8b874119efc705affe340e5d8ddd72170b2732b44cd67d624942232"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-28.png", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "", "sha256": "a78228bb228076950e8920a729909cf1ed38f0effc05990b6a0070607a0b6eeb"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.txt", "line_start": 1038, "line_end": 1042, "quote": "18\n\n                                                                                       (2.25)\n\nWhere         and         are obtained using relations similar to (2.20). Note that similar to", "sha256": "ba0fdee00337a3e1f5cdb075ac6523d9a81101942aa324fb8498e13dd928eb25"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.txt", "line_start": 1088, "line_end": 1101, "quote": "\n\n                                                                                           19\n\nthe total depth averaged velocity and surface elevation due to the incident waves is given\nby\n\n\n                                                                                         (2.27)\n\nAssuming that the wave form remains constant along the individual wave rays each of the\nharmonics obeys\n\n", "sha256": "ba0fdee00337a3e1f5cdb075ac6523d9a81101942aa324fb8498e13dd928eb25"}], "closure_status": "documented_limit", "note": "Outgoing shallow-water characteristic assumption: x is positive inward by the boundary-coordinate paragraph, hence the displayed -c characteristic travels outward. Reflected waves are assumed long and normal to the straight boundary. This PDE is a derivation assumption; direct time-space stencil equivalence is not asserted. Association unchanged; object member identities are in relationship.member/ole.member, with the adapter top-level member null retained.", "symbol_definition_review": {"searched": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.txt (whole-document textual search for definition/denotes/index/time-step/averaging/interpolation terms), nomenclature images pp.6-7, relevant equation and adjacent defining images, and computation-sequence images pp.32-33 for time labels", "remaining_undefined": ["r (reflected)"], "interpretation": "No definition was replaced by introductory/derivation prose. Standard meaning from source/context alone is recorded as a document limit; unresolved is retained where the equation meaning or implementation is unexplained."}}
{"id": "nonhydro:word:112501", "association": {"status": "unique", "objects": [{"member": null, "locator": {"container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "xml_ordinal": 16953, "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 16924}, "relationship": {"id": "rId523", "target": "embeddings/oleObject247.bin", "type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/oleObject", "member": "word/embeddings/oleObject247.bin"}, "ole": {"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx!word/embeddings/oleObject247.bin", "storage": "zip-member", "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "member": "word/embeddings/oleObject247.bin", "sha256": "e9a7ca9d3d7fcc9020e332f68f3d170011b41362e7ff75b8475e57620d5397ea"}, "previews": [{"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx!word/media/image227.wmf", "storage": "zip-member", "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "member": "word/media/image227.wmf", "sha256": "d7da5a60351f00fa2da157308b9efd7d1299952ba1e830c879754bc813a2d1d7", "relationship": {"id": "rId524", "target": "media/image227.wmf", "type": "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image", "member": "word/media/image227.wmf"}, "xml_ordinal": 16952}]}], "page": 30}, "body_status": "readable", "equation_content": {"images_used": [{"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-30.png", "region": "(2.35) equation body, physical render page 30", "sha256": "813ea130b966030d72267a06c91e0cd960c1977025c3b7ba04e798bef60f4f31"}, {"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-f