he grid has a wavelength of. If we define a shallow water wave as a wave for which  then the smallest wave has become a shallow water wave when the depth is:", "meaning": "threshold defining a shallow water wave by kH<(kH)_min; default zero specified in paragraph 16961"}], "evidence": [{"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 974, "line_end": 1039, "quote": "      ! Determine whether or not to use the nh correction method (dry/wet/breaking etc.)\n      !\n      if(par%useXBeachGSettings==0 .or. par%nhbreaker<=1) then\n         call nonh_break( s , par )\n      else\n         ! (1)  The point is dry\n         ! (2)  The relative wave length kd of the smallest possible wave (L=2dx) is smaller than kdmin\n         ! (3)  The interpolated waterlevel zs is below the bottom (steep cliffs with overwash situations)\n         ! (4)  Where Miche breaker criterium applies -> bores are hydrostatic\n         !            max steepness = H/L = maxbrsteep\n         !            dz/dx = maxbrsteep\n         !            dz/dx = dz/dt/c = w/c = w/sqrt(gh)\n         !            wmax = maxbrsteep*sqrt(gh)\n         do j=1,s%ny+1\n            do i=1,s%nx+1\n               iw = max(i,i-1)\n               ie = min(s%nx,i+1)\n               iee = min(s%nx,i+2)\n\n               if (  (s%wetU(i,j)==1                                      )  &\n               .and. (0.5_rKind*(s%zs(i,j) + s%zs(ie,j))    > zbu(i,j)    )  &\n               .and. ( s%dsu(i,1)*par%kdmin/par%px  < s%hum(i,j)  )  ) then\n                  nonhU(i,j) = 1\n               else\n                  nonhU(i,j) = 0\n               endif\n            enddo\n         enddo\n\n         if (s%ny>2) then\n            do j=1,s%ny+1\n               js = min(s%ny,j+1)\n               do i=1,s%nx+1\n                  if (  (s%wetV(i,j)==1                                      )  &\n                  .and. (0.5_rKind*(s%zs(i,j) + s%zs(i,js))    > zbv(i,j)    )  &\n                  .and. ( s%dnv(1,j)*par%kdmin/par%px  < s%hvm(i,j)  )  ) then\n                     nonhV(i,j) = 1\n                  else\n                     nonhV(i,j) = 0\n                  endif\n               enddo\n            enddo\n         else\n            nonhV = 0\n         endif\n         !\n         ! Determine if a velocity point will be included in the nonh pressure matrix, include if\n         ! any of the surrounding velocity points is included.\n         !\n         if (s%ny>0) then\n            do j=2,s%ny\n               do i=2,s%nx\n                  if (max(nonhV(i,j),nonhV(i,j-1),nonhU(i,j),nonhU(i-1,j)) > 0) then\n                     nonhZ(i,j) = 1\n                  else\n                     nonhZ(i,j) = 0\n                  endif\n               enddo\n            enddo\n         else\n            do i=2,s%nx\n               if (max(nonhU(i,1),nonhU(i-1,1)) > 0) then\n                  nonhZ(i,1) = 1\n               else\n                  nonhZ(i,1) = 0\n               endif", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 3097, "line_end": 3145, "quote": "      ! Determine if a velocity point will be included in the nonh pressure matrix, do not include if:\n      !\n      ! (1)  The point is dry\n      ! (2)  The relative wave length kd of the smallest possible wave (L=2dx) is smaller than kdmin\n      ! (3)  The interpolated waterlevel zs is below the bottom (steep cliffs with overwash situations)\n      ! (4)  Where Miche breaker criterium applies -> bores are hydrostatic\n      !            max steepness = H/L = maxbrsteep\n      !            dz/dx = maxbrsteep\n      !            dz/dx = dz/dt/c = w/c = w/sqrt(gh)\n      !            wmax = maxbrsteep*sqrt(gh)\n\n      !\n      do j=1,s%ny+1\n         !\n         do i=1,s%nx+1\n            !\n            ie = min(s%nx,i+1)\n            !\n            if (  (s%wetU(i,j)==1 ) .and. ( 0.5_rKind*( s%zs(i,j) + s%zs(ie,j) ) > zbu(i,j) ) ) then\n               !\n               nonhU(i,j) = 1\n               !\n            else\n               !\n               nonhU(i,j) = 0\n               !\n            endif\n            !\n         enddo\n         !\n      enddo\n\n      !\n      if (s%ny>2) then\n         !\n         do j=1,s%ny+1\n            !\n            js = min(s%ny,j+1)\n            !\n            do i=1,s%nx+1\n               !\n               if (  (s%wetV(i,j)==1 ) .and. (0.5_rKind*(s%zs(i,j) + s%zs(i,js)) > zbv(i,j) ) ) then\n                  !\n                  nonhV(i,j) = 1\n                  !\n               else\n                  !\n                  nonhV(i,j) = 0\n                  !", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 3163, "line_end": 3177, "quote": "      do j=jmin_zs,jmax_zs\n         !\n         js = max( j-1 , 1 )\n         !\n         do i=imin_zs,imax_zs\n            !\n            if (max( nonhV(i,j) , nonhV(i,js) ,nonhU(i,j), nonhU(i-1,j)) > 0) then\n               !\n               nonhZ(i,j) = 1\n               !\n            else\n               !\n               nonhZ(i,j) = 0\n               !\n            endif", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 674, "line_end": 677, "quote": "               else\n                  mat(1  ,i,j) = 1.0_rKind\n                  mat(2:5,i,j) = 0.0_rKind\n                  rhs(i,j)     = 0.0_rKind", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/params.F90", "line_start": 895, "line_end": 895, "quote": "         par%kdmin        = readkey_dbl('params.txt','kdmin' ,0.0d0,0.0d0,0.05d0)", "sha256": "73648b5733a8f90a8f18cda32743bdc2ef42f649e39c521e28e06584ee63c359"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 233, "line_end": 243, "quote": "       case default\n         !\n         ! The \"old\" code is used\n         !\n         if ( ipredcor == 0 ) then\n            ! -- Predictor\n            call nonh_1lay_pred(s,par)\n            !\n         else\n            ! -- Corrector\n            call nonh_1lay_cor(s,par)", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.txt", "line_start": 1172, "line_end": 1185, "quote": "\n\nPressure points are considered dry when all of the surrounding velocity points are dry. When\nthis is the case the pressure point is no longer included in the computations and the main\ndiagonal of the linear system is set to one while the right hand side is set to zero.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                           21\n\nFigure 3-8 (a) A velocity point is considered dry if the total water depth is under a certain threshold. (b) A water\nlevel point is considered wet if any of the surrounding velocity points are wet, even if the water depth itself is below\nthe threshold.", "sha256": "ba0fdee00337a3e1f5cdb075ac6523d9a81101942aa324fb8498e13dd928eb25"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "(i) Water depth", "sha256": "8ff30d98c3ba928f3b28f556e10a978973d6e4e25c8ea928da648775c6227318"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "Local mesh interval in x-direction", "sha256": "8ff30d98c3ba928f3b28f556e10a978973d6e4e25c8ea928da648775c6227318"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "(ii) Wave number  ", "sha256": "8ff30d98c3ba928f3b28f556e10a978973d6e4e25c8ea928da648775c6227318"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/manual-notes/xbeach-nonhydrostatic-report-2010.md", "line_start": 139, "line_end": 145, "quote": "- Dry points receive zero velocity and a pressure equation with diagonal '1' and right-hand side '0', while higher-order reconstruction requires all three stencil surface levels to exceed all three bed levels.\n- Dry velocity points are set to zero, fully dry pressure rows use diagonal 1 and right-hand side 0, higher-order reconstruction is disabled unless the lowest stencil surface exceeds the highest bed, and shallow-water pressure-point removal defaults to zero.\n\n**출처 locator:**\n\n- XH169: non-hydrostatic_report_draft.doc, DOC/DOCX→동일 work PDF 정렬, physical PDF p.29, 30, printed page/frontmatter 19, 20, audit extract lines 1205-1242; 원본 SHA-256 `07428e686eb4d2211448dcae7b7f77cdae8281affa020f68dacf42df19aa19ec`.\n- XH189: non-hydrostatic_report_draft.pdf, 직접 PDF, physical PDF p.29, 30, printed page/frontmatter 19, 20, audit extract lines 2914-2927; 원본 SHA-256 `d170530492ec5f4052f450eec28f7965ae44ac10276248e24cad41b5f6e41005`.", "sha256": "bd4a1687c42001692e30c8a5a165dfcd0a7d5ba1e83ced6c17301645db6995f3"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-06.png", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "List of Main symbols", "sha256": "1cd46d9a237e9ddede36b24afb8e5e7b7f706abd687d5093717879815f73950c"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/pages/page-07.png", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "List of Main symbols", "sha256": "167a275bb8b874119efc705affe340e5d8ddd72170b2732b44cd67d624942232"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "(2.35)", "sha256": "8ff30d98c3ba928f3b28f556e10a978973d6e4e25c8ea928da648775c6227318"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "If the local water depth is relatively small most waves of practical interest have become shallow water waves. From a numerical point of view the smallest wave that can be represented on the grid has a wavelength of. If we define a shallow water wave as a wave for which  then the smallest wave has become a shallow water wave when the depth is:", "sha256": "8ff30d98c3ba928f3b28f556e10a978973d6e4e25c8ea928da648775c6227318"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "If  then it appears appropriate to disable the calculation of the non-hydrostatic pressure by removing the point from the linear system in a similar way as for a dry point. Removing these points might improve the convergence rate and stability of the pressure correction algorithm. Presently it appears that for low values of  there is hardly any difference in simulations without the removal of these points. For this reason the default value of  is set to zero, which practically means that points are never removed for this reason.", "sha256": "8ff30d98c3ba928f3b28f556e10a978973d6e4e25c8ea928da648775c6227318"}], "closure_status": "resolved", "note": "Grid-resolvability depth cutoff: k=π/Δx from λ=2Δx. In the one-layer legacy branch reached only when useXBeachGSettings!=0 and nhbreaker>1, nonhU is enabled if dsu*kdmin/px<hum, and nonhV analogously uses dnv/hvm; pressure nonhZ is included if any surrounding velocity mask is enabled. kdmin defaults to 0. Equality is excluded in the code although the document states removal for H<H_threshold. The normal useXBeachGSettings==0 or nhbreaker<=1 branch calls nonh_break, whose actual masks use wet flags and interpolated surface above bed without kdmin, despite its comment mentioning kdmin. Inactive rows are identity with zero RHS. These are explained branch/threshold differences, not an unlocated implementation. H_threshold is defined by (2.35), and (kH)_min is the explicit shallow-wave criterion in paragraph 16865; paragraph 16961 states the removal rule and zero default."}

