VERDICT {"id": "kingsday:xml:97449", "verdict": "REFUTED", "field": "equation_content.transcription; symbols[q_gw^x,q_gw^y].definition_quote; reviewer_note", "problem": "B.24 likewise prints Delta z_{u,i} and Delta z_{v,i}, each twice, without j. The transcription supplies j in all four places. Its reused B.23 definition quotes repeat the same error. The parabolic-head and conductivity corrections otherwise withstand comparison.", "evidence": ["R:7", "IMG/page-133.png, B.24, directly inspected and enlarged", "IMG/page-132.png, B.23", "SRC/groundwater.F90:907-915,1285-1287,1303-1321,1429-1433"], "fix": "Preserve the omitted j in B.24 and the reused B.23 quotes. Retain the printed i+1,j y-gradient, the corrected conductivity conditions, and unresolved closure."}
VERDICT {"id": "kingsday:xml:103051", "verdict": "REFUTED", "field": "equation_content.transcription; symbols; evidence_origin; note", "problem": "B.57's final y-average is mistranscribed. Both RHS q terms have x index i+1/2, not respectively i and i+1. The asserted printed stencil in the explanation repeats this error.", "evidence": ["_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/kingsday/page-142.png, B.57 final row, directly inspected at enlarged scale", "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/verify2/W-06.jsonl:10"], "fix": "Use ^y q̄^{n+1/2}_{i+1/2,j+1/2}=1/2(^y q^{n+1/2}_{i+1/2,j+1/2}+^y q^{n+1/2}_{i+1/2,j-1/2}). Update all copied definitions and explanations. Preserve this printed stencil without inferring an intended repair; retain unresolved."}
VERDICT {"id": "kingsday:xml:104682", "verdict": "REFUTED", "field": "equation_content.transcription; reviewer_note; evidence_origin", "problem": "The first numerator drops a printed index: the predicted term is W̄*_{i,j,1}, not W̄*_{i,j}. This anomalous extra face index must be preserved.", "evidence": ["_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/kingsday/display-recovered/page-145.png, B.67 first numerator, directly inspected at enlarged scale", "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/verify2/W-06.jsonl:20"], "fix": "Restore W̄*_{i,j,1}; record the printed index asymmetry without silently reconciling it with B.64. Keep the analogous-construction reference and unresolved implementation closure."}
VERDICT {"id": "master:xml:96732", "verdict": "REFUTED", "field": "equation_content.transcription; document_observations; symbols; evidence[0].quote; evidence_origin[new_comparison].claims_resolved", "problem": "Both viscosity factors in the U_y bracket carry DOUBLE overbars in the printed image. The transcription uses single-bar ν̄ and document_observations expressly claims a single bar there. The adjacent linear-interpolation definition for doubly barred quantities is also unlinked. Additionally, the stored document quote still describes boundary-condition output files.", "evidence": ["_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/verify2/W-11.jsonl:29", "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/master/page-144.png: C.54, second bracket, both ν factors; immediately following interpolation paragraph", "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx!word/document.xml@96784: surrounding-point linear-interpolation definition", "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/master/display-recovered/render.txt:7504-7514, LF/newline numbering", "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/correct2/R2-09.changes.jsonl:72"], "fix": "Change both U_y-bracket ν̄ factors to ν̿ and remove the asserted single/double-bar distinction. Link the interpolation definition at @96784, preserving its printed indices. Re-extract the correct document quote and revise provenance claims. Keep the confirmed mixed time levels, i+1½ subscript, conditional source comparison and unresolved closure."}
VERDICT {"id": "nonhydro:word:106173", "verdict": "REFUTED", "field": "equation_content.transcription; symbols", "problem": "Both derivatives in printed (2.30) use lowercase u^r, but the transcription substitutes uppercase U^r and supplies the uppercase-U definition. This silently removes a document notation change.", "evidence": "D/pages/page-28.png (2.30), enlarged equation region x=155..480,y=1060..1135, clearly shows lowercase u^r. The following (2.31) visibly uses uppercase U^r.", "fix": "Transcribe ∂u^r/∂t−c∂u^r/∂x=0. Record the lowercase/uppercase variation and link the local reflected-wave context without asserting an explicit global u=U identity. Retain the derivation-assumption classification."}
VERDICT {"id": "nonhydro:word:112501", "verdict": "REFUTED", "field": "equation_content.transcription; symbols", "problem": "The equation and nomenclature print uppercase X in ΔX, but the record transcribes Δx and explicitly describes the nomenclature entry as Δx_i.", "evidence": "D/pages/page-30.png (2.35), enlarged region x=155..570,y=1370..1455, prints ΔX/π. D/pages/page-07.png, local-mesh-interval entry, prints ΔX_i.", "fix": "Restore ΔX in the transcription and corresponding symbol/definition descriptions. Preserve the corrected threshold definitions, legacy-branch restriction and equality difference; the source comparison itself stands."}
