symbols [{"symbol": "q_gw^x", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 97215, "render_image": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/kingsday/page-132.png", "definition_basis": "printed defining equation or symbol-bearing clause"}, "definition_quote": "q_gw,i,j^x=-K_u,i,j Δz_u,i,j (H_i+1,j-H_i,j)/Δx_u,i,j=-K_u,i,j Δz_u,i,j (H_bc,i+1,j-H_bc,i,j)/Δx_u,i,j", "meaning": "horizontal groundwater discharge x component, defined by B.23; x/u directions named at paragraph 97300"}, {"symbol": "q_gw^y", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 97215, "render_image": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/kingsday/page-132.png", "definition_basis": "printed defining equation or symbol-bearing clause"}, "definition_quote": "q_gw,i,j^y=-K_v,i,j Δz_v,i,j (H_i+1,j-H_i,j)/Δy_v,i,j=-K_v,i,j Δz_v,i,j (H_bc,i+1,j-H_bc,i,j)/Δy_v,i,j", "meaning": "horizontal groundwater discharge y component, defined by B.23; the printed i+1,j neighbor remains distinct from the direction definition"}, {"symbol": "K", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 24669}, "definition_quote": "K is the hydraulic conductivity of the medium (keyword: kx, ky, kz, for each horizontal and vertical direction)", "meaning": "hydraulic conductivity; directional keyword correspondence is explicit"}, {"symbol": "Δz_u", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 96862, "render_image": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/kingsday/page-132.png", "definition_basis": "printed defining equation or symbol-bearing clause"}, "definition_quote": "Δz_u,i,j={Δz_H,i+1,j if q_gw,i,j^x<0; Δz_H,i,j if q_gw,i,j^x≥0}", "meaning": "upwind groundwater cell height at the u interface, defined by B.21"}, {"symbol": "Δz_v", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 96862, "render_image": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/kingsday/page-132.png", "definition_basis": "printed defining equation or symbol-bearing clause"}, "definition_quote": "Δz_v,i,j={Δz_H,i+1,j if q_gw,i,j^y<0; Δz_H,i,j if q_gw,i,j^y≥0}", "meaning": "upwind groundwater cell height at the v interface, defined by B.21; the printed i+1,j on the y-flow branch is retained"}, {"symbol": "H", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 24669}, "definition_quote": "H is the hydraulic head", "meaning": "hydraulic head; paragraph 25494 further names the mean vertical groundwater head"}, {"symbol": "H_bc", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 96947}, "definition_quote": "the head applied on the top boundary of the groundwater domain (Hbc)", "meaning": "groundwater top-boundary hydraulic head"}, {"symbol": "Δx_u", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "Δy_v", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "i,j", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 94025}, "definition_quote": "The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction", "meaning": "flow/sediment grid indices in u and v directions"}, {"symbol": "u,v", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 97300}, "definition_quote": "the subscripts u and v refer to variables approximated at the horizontal cell interfaces in the cross-shore and longshore direction, respectively", "meaning": "cross-shore and longshore face locations"}, {"symbol": "x,y", "definition_locator": {"container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "paragraph_xml_ordinal": 97300}, "definition_quote": "the superscripts x and y refer to the components of the variable in the cross-shore and longshore direction, respectively", "meaning": "cross-shore and longshore components"}]
note "Darcy horizontal velocities use -K*headgrad and face fluxes multiply by gwhu/gwhv. Gradient spacings are dsu/dnv. Differences: The y line of the image uses i+1,j in both head differences; code uses i,j+1. Hydrostatic head is averaged with the preceding head rather than set exactly to H_bc. gwnonh selects the groundwater pressure path (:373-382). gw_solver receives Kxupd/Kyupd/Kzupd (:382); gw_calculate_velocities receives separate Kx/Ky/Kz inputs (:397), reset to par%kx/par%ky/par%kz after each step (:415-417). Inside that routine Kxupd/Kyupd/Kzupd are intent(out) (:1287) and are overwritten with Kx/Ky/Kz (:1303-1305). Its Kin arguments are Kx/Ky/Kz (:1311-1329), not the conductivity supplied to the solver. isnonh is supplied by par%wavemodel==WAVEMODEL_NONH, independently of gwnonh. Laminar horizontal velocity uses Kin; turbulent horizontal velocity uses Kin in that surface-wave nonhydrostatic mode and otherwise its locally recomputed Kupd (:1429-1433). Interface heights and dry-cell caps modify the fluxes. Open: B.23 defines q_gw^x/y and B.21 defines the Δz interface heights. The printed y-neighbor discrepancy remains unresolved. Definition locators refer only to explicit naming/defining clauses; no defining meaning is inferred from introductory prose. Unbound exact notation uses undefined_in_document. Groundwater physical η and η_gw definitions are cited; any ζ, δ/d, H_gw/H or q pressure/flux variants remain distinct as recorded. Association object top-level member is null as in the packet adapter shape; the actual original member, relationship, locator, preview hashes and OLE hash are preserved in the nested object. S1 correction: q_gw^x, q_gw^y, Δz_u, Δz_v now link to explicit defining clauses/equations; formerly claimed missing definitions for these symbols are withdrawn. Remaining gaps concern the literal variants listed under search_scope.symbol_definitions and the stated model/implementation issues. S3: gwnonh selects the groundwater pressure path (:373-382). gw_solver receives Kxupd/Kyupd/Kzupd (:382); gw_calculate_velocities receives separate Kx/Ky/Kz inputs (:397), reset to par%kx/par%ky/par%kz after each step (:415-417). Inside that routine Kxupd/Kyupd/Kzupd are intent(out) (:1287) and are overwritten with Kx/Ky/Kz (:1303-1305). Its Kin arguments are Kx/Ky/Kz (:1311-1329), not the conductivity supplied to the solver. isnonh is supplied by par%wavemodel==WAVEMODEL_NONH, independently of gwnonh. Laminar horizontal velocity uses Kin; turbulent horizontal velocity uses Kin in that surface-wave nonhydrostatic mode and otherwise its locally recomputed Kupd (:1429-1433). Comment/code mismatch: groundwater.F90:387-396 claims velocity uses the Poisson-solver conductivity estimate. The actual call at :397 supplies base Kx/Ky/Kz as Kin, while :1287 declares updated arrays intent(out) and :1303-1305 overwrites them; therefore the incoming pressure-solver Kxupd/Kyupd/Kzupd estimate does not determine the velocity conductivity. The comments at :370 and :1430 make the same unsupported claim. Which conductivity best serves the intended coupled method and its conservation consequences are not resolved here."
closure_status "unresolved"
implementation_relation "mapped_with_differences"
