l differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "meaning": "depth-averaged y velocity"}, {"symbol": "Δx", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "Δy", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "i", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "grid number in u direction"}, {"symbol": "j", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "grid number in v direction"}, {"symbol": "n", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "time-step index"}]
note "T/H maps to viscu: x normal strain, y U gradient and y divergence of V_x. Differences: source multiplies the initial normal component by 2 only for smag==1 and includes V_x cross term only for smag==1; uses metric spacings, wet masks and four-point ν averaging. ν is supplied by viscosity-off=0, Smagorinsky or par%nuh with nhbreaker-dependent increments, and subsequently scaled by nuhv before the vertical nonh predictor. Printed mixed-stage/time details are recorded as document observations; no exact stencil equality claimed. Source evidence locators: models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:365-404; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:411-464; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:496-496. No silent ν=ν_h, W=wind-speed W, or d=−zb document-definition substitution is made; source/context meaning is distinguished from missing document definition. Association unchanged. Packet objects have no top-level member field; member=null preserves that shape, while actual ZIP member, relationship, locator and hashes are retained in relationship/ole/previews. Independent correction: NARROWED confirmed against the opened equation page and source/context; 인용문을 재추출한다. 명시된 전사 불확실성과 구현 조건은 유지한다. S1 full-document text search plus visible nomenclature/defining-equation review: remaining undefined_in_document symbols are ν, Δx, Δy. Their standard meanings or supplied source context alone are documentation limits; substantive pressure, boundary, placement or implementation gaps remain unresolved where stated. Bare ν in the turbulent-stress equation is not silently identified with ν_h at @20451 or the water kinematic viscosity ν at @25292; those define different notation/context. The additional confirmed n+1/n+½ asymmetry in the transverse U and V factors is not explained by the source, which uses the supplied s%uu/s%vv fields at a single assembled stage (flow_timestep.F90:445-462). Thus exact literal mixed-stage stencil meaning remains unresolved even though central viscous terms have source counterparts."
