equation_content {"images_used": [{"path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/full-visual-read/master/page-144.png", "region": "Equation (C.54) at its printed caption; full existing render page", "sha256": "6f4e82cee387828dda3cbe768e6a3d196caa31f5d4d442b6987a00875abc4edc"}], "transcription": "{}^{x}T_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2} = (2/Δx_{i+1/2})[ν_{i+1,j}^{n}H_{i+1,j}^{n+1}(U_{i+1½,j}^{n+1/2}−U_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2})/Δx_{i+1} − ν_{i,j}^{n}H_{i,j}^{n+1}(U_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2}−U_{i−1/2,j}^{n+1/2})/Δx_i] + (1/Δy_i)[ν̄_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{n+1/2}H̿_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{n+1/2}(U_{i+1/2,j+1}^{n+1}−U_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2})/Δy_{i+1/2} − ν̄_{i+1/2,j−1/2}^{n+1/2}H̿_{i+1/2,j−1/2}^{n+1}(U_{i+1/2,j}^{n+1/2}−U_{i+1/2,j−1}^{n+1/2})/Δy_{i−1/2}] + (1/Δy_i)[ν̿_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{n+1/2}H̿_{i+1/2,j+1/2}^{n+1/2}(V_{i+1,j+1/2}^{n+1}−V_{i,j+1/2}^{n+1/2})/Δx_{i+1/2} − ν̿_{i+1/2,j−1/2}^{n+1/2}H̿_{i+1/2,j−1/2}^{n+1}(V_{i+1,j−1/2}^{n+1/2}−V_{i,j−1/2}^{n+1/2})/Δx_{i+1/2}]", "uncertain_symbols": [], "reviewer_note": "Reopened the listed existing page images with tools.view_image for this correction. This is a visual transcription, separate from the document-text quotes. Left superscripts are written {}^{x}, {}^{y}, {}^{w}, or {}^{u}; q is lowercase, q̄/W̄ have a single overbar and ν̿/H̿ a double overbar. Every printed time and spatial index is retained; no α/β abbreviation or normalization is used. Document observations: The first forward U and V factors in the two y brackets have n+1, while the backward factors have n+½. H double bars and different time levels n+½/n+1 are preserved. The ν overbar in the U_y bracket is single; in the V_x bracket it is double. The first U spatial subscript is printed i+1½. Δy_i and Δy_{i±½} are printed as such."}
document_observations ["The first forward U and V factors in the two y brackets have n+1, while the backward factors have n+½. H double bars and different time levels n+½/n+1 are preserved. The ν overbar in the U_y bracket is single; in the V_x bracket it is double. The first U spatial subscript is printed i+1½. Δy_i and Δy_{i±½} are printed as such."]
symbols [{"symbol": "T", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 96639, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here Pr represents a discretization of the dynamic pressure; T the effect of (turbulent) viscosity and S includes all other source terms. The discretization of the (turbulent) viscous terms is given by central differences:", "meaning": "turbulent/viscous contribution"}, {"symbol": "ν", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "H", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 95357, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "meaning": "water depth"}, {"symbol": "U", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 95357, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "meaning": "depth-averaged x velocity"}, {"symbol": "V", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 95357, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "meaning": "depth-averaged y velocity"}, {"symbol": "Δx", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "Δy", "definition_locator": null, "definition_quote": null, "meaning": "undefined_in_document"}, {"symbol": "i", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "grid number in u direction"}, {"symbol": "j", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "grid number in v direction"}, {"symbol": "n", "definition_locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}, "definition_quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "meaning": "time-step index"}]
evidence_origin [{"origin": "new_comparison", "ref": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/master_xml_96732.json", "claims_resolved": ["Actual visual body at (C.54); document text quotes and defining symbol links rechecked", "Bounded source comparison with the term/stage/sign limits stated in note"], "gaps_left": ["T/H maps to viscu: x normal strain, y U gradient and y divergence of V_x. Differences: source multiplies the initial normal component by 2 only for smag==1 and includes V_x cross term only for smag==1; uses metric spacings, wet masks and four-point ν averaging. ν is supplied by viscosity-off=0, Smagorinsky or par%nuh with nhbreaker-dependent increments, and subsequently scaled by nuhv before the vertical nonh predictor. Printed mixed-stage/time details are recorded as document observations; no exact stencil equality claimed. Source evidence locators: models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:365-404; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:411-464; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:496-496. No silent ν=ν_h, W=wind-speed W, or d=−zb document-definition substitution is made; source/context meaning is distinguished from missing document definition. Association unchanged. Packet objects have no top-level member field; member=null preserves that shape, while actual ZIP member, relationship, locator and hashes are retained in relationship/ole/previews. Independent correction: NARROWED confirmed against the opened equation page and source/context; 인용문을 재추출한다. 명시된 전사 불확실성과 구현 조건은 유지한다. S1 full-document text search plus visible nomenclature/defining-equation review: remaining undefined_in_document symbols are ν, Δx, Δy. Their standard meanings or supplied source context alone are documentation limits; substantive pressure, boundary, placement or implementation gaps remain unresolved where stated. Bare ν in the turbulent-stress equation is not silently identified with ν_h at @20451 or the water kinematic viscosity ν at @25292; those define different notation/context. The additional confirmed n+1/n+½ asymmetry in the transverse U and V factors is not explained by the source, which uses the supplied s%uu/s%vv fields at a single assembled stage (flow_timestep.F90:445-462). Thus exact literal mixed-stage stencil meaning remains unresolved even though central viscous terms have source counterparts."]}, {"origin": "existing_contract", "ref": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/build-mode-20260912/contracts.json#/modes/3", "claims_resolved": ["WAVEMODEL_NONH/nonhq3d!=1 dispatches old one-layer predictor then UV advection correction then pressure corrector"], "gaps_left": ["This dispatch contract does not adjudicate individual equation terms, indices, signs or coefficients"]}]
note "T/H maps to viscu: x normal strain, y U gradient and y divergence of V_x. Differences: source multiplies the initial normal component by 2 only for smag==1 and includes V_x cross term only for smag==1; uses metric spacings, wet masks and four-point ν averaging. ν is supplied by viscosity-off=0, Smagorinsky or par%nuh with nhbreaker-dependent increments, and subsequently scaled by nuhv before the vertical nonh predictor. Printed mixed-stage/time details are recorded as document observations; no exact stencil equality claimed. Source evidence locators: models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:365-404; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:411-464; models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90:496-496. No silent ν=ν_h, W=wind-speed W, or d=−zb document-definition substitution is made; source/context meaning is distinguished from missing document definition. Association unchanged. Packet objects have no top-level member field; member=null preserves that shape, while actual ZIP member, relationship, locator and hashes are retained in relationship/ole/previews. Independent correction: NARROWED confirmed against the opened equation page and source/context; 인용문을 재추출한다. 명시된 전사 불확실성과 구현 조건은 유지한다. S1 full-document text search plus visible nomenclature/defining-equation review: remaining undefined_in_document symbols are ν, Δx, Δy. Their standard meanings or supplied source context alone are documentation limits; substantive pressure, boundary, placement or implementation gaps remain unresolved where stated. Bare ν in the turbulent-stress equation is not silently identified with ν_h at @20451 or the water kinematic viscosity ν at @25292; those define different notation/context. The additional confirmed n+1/n+½ asymmetry in the transverse U and V factors is not explained by the source, which uses the supplied s%uu/s%vv fields at a single assembled stage (flow_timestep.F90:445-462). Thus exact literal mixed-stage stencil meaning remains unresolved even though central viscous terms have source counterparts."
EVIDENCE [{"role": "document_text", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/manuals-docx-read/master/display-recovered/render.txt", "line_start": 7504, "line_end": 7514, "quote": "      transitions between the boundary condition files may affect the model results.\n      Every time the XBeach wave boundary condition module is run, it outputs data to the local\n      directory. Metadata about the wave boundary conditions are stored in list files: ebcflist.bcf and\n      qbcflist.bcf. The main XBeach program uses the list files to know how and when to read and\n      generate boundary condition files. The actual incoming short-wave energy and long-wave\n      mass flux data is stored in other files. These files have E_ and q_ prefixes. The main XBeach\n      program uses these files for the actual forcing along the offshore edge.\n\n\n\n", "sha256": "3a455dff9ca9050757471e774527dd569733659c89b8a5961c3b25e0c195092d"}, {"role": "receipt", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/r2-20261001/packets/master_xml_96732.json", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 12, "quote": "{\n  \"schema\": \"xbeach-r2-evidence-packet/v1\",\n  \"caption\": {\n    \"id\": \"master:xml:96732\",\n    \"document\": \"master\",\n    \"label\": \"(C.54)\",\n    \"locator_kind\": \"start_xml_ordinal\",\n    \"locator\": 96732,\n    \"source\": {\n      \"path\": \"models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx\",\n      \"sha256\": \"9f142b89e0659e71066054c3d61b4d6f29ba3c10c5984e26e9a2d37d2fae3236\"\n    },", "sha256": "5bd64e03e928694f5217e0d1b71a8c1aeca68eee9a0fc125053e6060cb1094db"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90", "line_start": 365, "line_end": 404, "quote": "      ! There is a possibility to turn viscosity off\n      if (par%viscosity==0) then ! Dano: put it here so it actualy saves a lot of computation time\n         s%nuh = 0.d0\n         s%viscu = 0.d0\n      else\n\n         ! Jaap: Slightly changes approach; 1) background viscosity is user defined or obtained from Smagorinsky, 2) nuh = max(nuh,roller induced viscosity)\n         if (par%smag == 1) then\n            !Use smagorinsky subgrid model\n            call visc_smagorinsky(s,par)\n         else\n            s%nuh = par%nuh\n         endif\n         !\n         ! Add viscosity for wave breaking effects\n         if (par%swave == 1) then\n            if (par%smag==0) then ! approach of Reniers seems inconsistent with Smagorinski\n               do j=j1,max(s%ny,1)\n                  do i=2,s%nx\n                     s%nuh(i,j) = max(s%nuh(i,j),par%nuhfac*s%hh(i,j)*(s%DR(i,j)/par%rho)**(1.0d0/3.0d0)) ! Ad: change to max\n                  end do\n               end do\n            endif\n         elseif (par%swave==0 .and. par%wavemodel==WAVEMODEL_NONH) then\n            select case (par%nhbreaker)\n             case (1)\n               where (s%breaking/=0)\n                  s%nuh = par%breakviscfac*s%nuh\n               endwhere\n             case (2)\n               where (s%breaking==1)\n                  s%nuh = s%nuh + (par%nuh*par%breakvisclen*s%hh)**2*sqrt(dudx**2+dvdy**2)\n               endwhere\n             case (3)\n               ! Ad en Arnold: Battjes 1975 formulation to smoothen front of lf wave bore in the swash\n               ! compute (long) wave turbulence due to breaking\n               !nuh = max(par%nuh, par%avis*hloc*sqrt(kturb))\n             case default\n               ! do nothing to increase viscosity\n            end select", "sha256": "50742b601cc8feccd513cf742ca772b6021f1d4f5ffe074c4e8ffc90907dd2b2"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90", "line_start": 411, "line_end": 464, "quote": "               dudx1 = s%nuh(i+1,j)*s%hh(i+1,j)*(s%uu(i+1,j)-s%uu(i,j))/s%dsz(i+1,j)\n               dudx2 = s%nuh(i,j)  *s%hh(i  ,j)*(s%uu(i,j)-s%uu(i-1,j))/s%dsz(i,j)\n               s%viscu(i,j) = (1.0d0/s%hum(i,j))*( 2*(dudx1-dudx2)/(s%dsz(i,j)+s%dsz(i+1,j)) )\n            end do\n         end do\n\n         if (par%smag == 1) then\n            !\n            !   For non constant eddy viscosity the stress terms read:\n            !\n            !   d           d           d      d         d\n            !   -- [ 2* mu -- (U) ]  + --[ mu --(U) +mu --(V) ]\n            !   dx         dx          dy     dy        dx\n            !\n            !                d         d\n            !   Only when   -- [mu] = --[mu] = 0 we have (for incompressible flow)\n            !               dx        dy\n            !\n            !         2            2\n            !        d            d\n            !    mu --2 [U] + mu --2 [U]\n            !       dx           dy\n            !\n            s%viscu = 2.0d0*s%viscu\n         endif\n\n         do j=jmin_uu,jmax_uu\n            jp1=min(j+1,s%ny+1)\n            jm1=max(j-1,1)\n            do i=imin_uu,imax_uu\n               !Nuh is defined at eta points, interpolate from four surrounding points\n               nuh1  = .25d0*(s%nuh(i,j)+s%nuh(i+1,j)+s%nuh(i+1,jp1)+s%nuh(i,jp1))\n               nuh2  = .25d0*(s%nuh(i,j)+s%nuh(i+1,j)+s%nuh(i+1,jm1)+s%nuh(i,jm1))\n\n               dudy1 = nuh1 *.5d0*(s%hvm(i,j  )+s%hvm(i+1,j  ))*(s%uu(i,jp1)-s%uu(i,j))/s%dnc(i,j)\n               dudy2 = nuh2 *.5d0*(s%hvm(i,jm1)+s%hvm(i+1,jm1))*(s%uu(i,j)-s%uu(i,jm1))/s%dnc(i,jm1)\n               s%viscu(i,j) = s%viscu(i,j) + (1.0d0/s%hum(i,j))* &\n               ( 2.0d0*(dudy1-dudy2)/(s%dnc(i,j)+s%dnc(i,jm1)) )*s%wetu(i,jp1)*s%wetu(i,jm1)\n            end do\n         end do\n\n         if (par%smag == 1) then\n            do j=jmin_uu,jmax_uu\n               jp1=min(j+1,s%ny+1)\n               jm1=max(j-1,1)\n               do i=imin_uu,imax_uu\n                  !Nuh is defined at eta points, interpolate from four surrounding points\n                  nuh1  = .25d0*(s%nuh(i,j)+s%nuh(i+1,j)+s%nuh(i+1,jp1)+s%nuh(i,jp1))\n                  nuh2  = .25d0*(s%nuh(i,j)+s%nuh(i+1,j)+s%nuh(i+1,jm1)+s%nuh(i,jm1))\n\n                  dvdx1 = nuh1*.5d0*(s%hvm(i,j  )+s%hvm(i+1,j  ))*(s%vv(i+1,j  )-s%vv(i,j  ))/s%dsc(i,j)\n                  dvdx2 = nuh2*.5d0*(s%hvm(i,jm1)+s%hvm(i+1,jm1))*(s%vv(i+1,jm1)-s%vv(i,jm1))/s%dsc(i,jm1)\n                  s%viscu(i,j) = s%viscu(i,j) + (1.d0/s%hum(i,j))*(dvdx1-dvdx2)/s%dnz(i,j)*real(s%wetv(i+1,j) &\n                  * s%wetv(i,j)*s%wetv(i+1,jm1)*s%wetv(i,jm1),8)", "sha256": "50742b601cc8feccd513cf742ca772b6021f1d4f5ffe074c4e8ffc90907dd2b2"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90", "line_start": 496, "line_end": 496, "quote": "         s%nuh = par%nuhv*s%nuh !Robert en Ap: increase s%nuh interaction in d2v/dx2", "sha256": "50742b601cc8feccd513cf742ca772b6021f1d4f5ffe074c4e8ffc90907dd2b2"}, {"role": "contract", "path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/build-mode-20260912/contracts.json", "line_start": 40, "line_end": 49, "quote": "      \"id\": \"nonh_one_layer\",\n      \"guard\": \"wavemodel==NONH and nonhq3d!=1\",\n      \"sequence\": [\n        \"flow\",\n        \"nonh_cor(0) -> nonh_1lay_pred\",\n        \"flow_secondorder_advUV\",\n        \"nonh_cor(1) -> nonh_1lay_cor\"\n      ],\n      \"update_guard\": \"each successful physics step; input validation turns secorder on\"\n    },", "sha256": "5cf1339c508a60d2bfaedc17f0863f16a155df70d45159f8de8dea3fd0f2a0f6"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/nonh.F90", "line_start": 233, "line_end": 243, "quote": "       case default\n         !\n         ! The \"old\" code is used\n         !\n         if ( ipredcor == 0 ) then\n            ! -- Predictor\n            call nonh_1lay_pred(s,par)\n            !\n         else\n            ! -- Corrector\n            call nonh_1lay_cor(s,par)", "sha256": "18f471b386e5905a78c98c24fc2f6252ae4fc66c9e2010665e5f35a59d324583"}, {"role": "source_code", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/src/xbeachlibrary/flow_timestep.F90", "line_start": 635, "line_end": 658, "quote": "      if (par%wavemodel==WAVEMODEL_NONH) then\n         !Do explicit predictor step with pressure\n         call nonh_cor(s,par,0,uu_old,vv_old)\n\n#ifdef USEMPI\n         call xmpi_shift_ee(s%uu)\n         call xmpi_shift_ee(s%vv)\n#endif\n      end if\n\n      if (par%secorder==1) then\n         !Call second order correction to the advection\n         call flow_secondorder_advUV(s,par,uu_old,vv_old)\n#ifdef USEMPI\n         call xmpi_shift_ee(s%uu)\n         call xmpi_shift_ee(s%vv)\n#endif\n      end if\n\n      if (par%wavemodel==WAVEMODEL_NONH) then\n         ! do non-hydrostatic pressure compensation to solve short waves\n         call nonh_cor(s,par,1,uu_old,vv_old)\n         ! note: MPI shift in subroutine nonh_cor\n      end if", "sha256": "50742b601cc8feccd513cf742ca772b6021f1d4f5ffe074c4e8ffc90907dd2b2"}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "Here Pr represents a discretization of the dynamic pressure; T the effect of (turbulent) viscosity and S includes all other source terms. The discretization of the (turbulent) viscous terms is given by central differences:", "sha256": "9f142b89e0659e71066054c3d61b4d6f29ba3c10c5984e26e9a2d37d2fae3236", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 96639, "kind": "paragraph"}}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "In which U is the depth averaged velocity vector in x, V in y, H the water depth. A simple semi-discretization of  using central differences for the space derivative and using the Hansen scheme for the coupling between velocity and free surface results in:", "sha256": "9f142b89e0659e71066054c3d61b4d6f29ba3c10c5984e26e9a2d37d2fae3236", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 95357, "kind": "paragraph"}}, {"role": "document_text", "path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "line_start": 1, "line_end": 1, "quote": "Here, Acell is the area of the cell around the cell center, zs is the surface elevation, uu is the u-velocity in the u-point, hu the water depth in the u-point and vv the v-velocity in the v-point. The indices i,j refer to the grid number in u resp. v direction; the index n refers to the time step.", "sha256": "9f142b89e0659e71066054c3d61b4d6f29ba3c10c5984e26e9a2d37d2fae3236", "locator": {"path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx", "member": "word/document.xml", "start_xml_ordinal": 88397, "kind": "paragraph"}}]

